(ASTRA INTEL  |  Unclassified // Training sample) Tj
T* (Unmanned Aerial Systems Capability Brief 2024) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. Purpose) Tj
T* (This brief outlines current unmanned aerial systems \(UAS\) roles in) Tj
T* (intelligence, surveillance and reconnaissance \(ISR\) and tactical strike.) Tj
T* (Group 2-3 UAS platforms provide persistent ISR coverage over contested) Tj
T* (littoral approaches without exposing aircrew to surface-to-air threats.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2. Force design) Tj
T* (A mixed fleet of medium-altitude long-endurance air vehicles and smaller) Tj
T* (tactical quadcopters is recommended for brigade and joint task force use.) Tj
T* (Attritable airframes should be stocked to absorb expected combat loss rates.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
5 0 obj
<< /Length 540 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
72 720 Td
16 TL
(3. Command and control) Tj
T* (Beyond visual line of sight operations require redundant C2 links,) Tj
T* (including SATCOM primary and line-of-sight radio as a fallback path.) Tj
T* (Ground control stations should implement STANAG 4586 interoperability) Tj
T* (so allied payloads and air vehicles can be retasked during coalition ops.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Lost-link procedures must include a documented return-to-home orbit and) Tj
T* (an automatic flight termination option over water or designated ranges.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
6 0 obj
<< /Length 531 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
72 720 Td
16 TL
(4. Sensors and payloads) Tj
T* (Electro-optical / infrared turrets remain the primary ISR payload.) Tj
T* (Synthetic aperture radar is required for weather-independent mapping of) Tj
T* (coastal movement corridors in the Indo-Pacific theatre.) Tj
T* (Electronic support measures can cue other sensors onto emitters of interest.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Strike variants may carry precision-guided munitions only under positive) Tj
T* (human authorisation. Autonomous target engagement is not authorised.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
7 0 obj
<< /Length 673 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
72 720 Td
16 TL
(5. Major applications) Tj
T* (Border and exclusive economic zone monitoring.) Tj
T* (Convoy overwatch and route reconnaissance for land manoeuvre units.) Tj
T* (Ship-to-shore surveillance during amphibious entry operations.) Tj
T* (Battle damage assessment after stand-off fires.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (6. Risks and limitations) Tj
T* (UAS are vulnerable to cheap electronic warfare and GNSS spoofing.) Tj
T* (High-bandwidth video is difficult to sustain under contested spectrum.) Tj
T* (Public airspace integration still constrains training sorties near cities.) Tj
T* (Weather, icing and icing-adjacent humidity reduce small-UAS endurance.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
8 0 obj
<< /Length 538 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
72 720 Td
16 TL
(7. Key organisations and systems) Tj
T* (MQ-9 Reaper and similar MALE types remain the theatre ISR workhorse.) Tj
T* (General Atomics Aeronautical Systems and allied industry partners supply) Tj
T* (airframes, while NATO working groups set payload interface standards.) Tj
T* (National geospatial agencies consume the resulting imagery products.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Dates of interest: capability refresh programmed for 2024-2026, with) Tj
T* (a follow-on attritable system decision expected in late 2026.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 348 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
72 720 Td
16 TL
(8. Summary) Tj
T* (Persistent ISR from Group 2-3 UAS is a force multiplier if C2 resilience,) Tj
T* (spectrum management and airspace integration are funded together.) Tj
T* (The recommended near-term focus is redundant datalinks, SAR payloads,) Tj
T* (and training for operations in GNSS-degraded environments.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
